      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>This corporation is organized to plan and carry out the Ride Across California. A multi-day event involving fifth grade students, and other persons in support of the students, riding bicycles across the southern portion of the State of California.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>The Ride Across California (RAC) was founded to give fifth graders a right-of-passage experience that would build self-confidence and a "can do" spirit before entering Middle School. The RAC was meant to create a "one for all and all for one" experience without the competitive consequences of a race.Other objectives of the ride are:-To teach every rider that worthwhile accomplishments are a personal matter and not a method of determining who is better, faster, or superior.-To show all participants that each individual must work hard to ensure the success of everyone.-To demonstrate that success for everyone is the measure of a satisfying trip or experience; -To have students and their families experience camping in a tent; and-To teach students that it takes a dedicated set of adults and cooperation from young persons to successfully move so many young people across the state safely.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
